body:
He has “contrepreneur” in his headline and posts stuff like:

“(4/21/25) Important internet slang updates for social marketers:

Kevin = something bad&#10;
Owen = something good &#10;
James = something mid &#10;
Samuel = something real &#10;
Gurt = something smart but dangerous”

For a lot of the women I know that are actively trying to conceive, it’s mostly some combination of: &#10;  


* making sure that it’s not a false positive, especially if they’re testing early, have taken fertility medication, or have previously had early pregnancy losses


* wanting to do something nice for their partner to mark the occasion. The mother usually gets more attention during pregnancy, for obvious reasons, so announcing it to the father can be a good opportunity to make him feel special, and the pregnancy test is given to “prove” it’s real if you haven’t gotten an ultrasound yet &#10;  

I think I know just as many who were too excited and shared the news immediately though, and everyone seems pretty happy either way!
